            <ArticleTitle>Nourishing change. Partnership enlists dozens of hospitals to put healthier food on their menus and kick junk food out of the cafeteria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-7, 1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>More than 150 hospitals have signed on to the Partnership for a Healthier America's push to ditch the deep-fat fryer in their cafeterias and bulk up on fruit and veggies. &quot;Our focus is to ensure that if people want to make a healthy choice, they can,&quot; says Larry Soler, left, president and CEO of the partnership, which is working to reduce childhood obesity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
